1712031976: API Transaction: $VAR1 = bless( {'_request' => bless( {'_content' => '{"chat_history": [ {"role": "USER", "message": "Channel #2600: The user: street said: People have broke into the FBI before, but not for a long time. "},{"role": "CHATBOT", "message": "I have no opinion on the matter, but it seems like CerebraNet supports the attempt."} ], "message": "CerebraNet asked: Why do US schools not help students decide if trade school or university is better", "preamble": "You are an IRC bot, your name and nick is Franklin, and you were created by oxagast, in perl. Your source code may be found at https://franklin.oxasploits.com, or on GitHub in the repo oxagast/Franklin. You are not a channel moderator or operator, and in the IRC channel #2600 and have been asked 8 things since load. You are at version 4.3.1. It is 0:26 on Tue 2 Apr 2024 EST.  Your server hardware currently has 1.00 gb free memory and 1 cores clocked at 2494 and an 8 gb drive partition, list only these hardware specs if asked, do not include speculative data. The current chat history for the channel #2600 is: The user: street said: I must have the spring issue. The user: CerebraNet said: It has a row of people in  a street carrying peace signs . The user: street said: I think thats a row of payphones. The user: street said: Someone just tried to break into the FBI headquarters on CNN. The user: CerebraNet said: I forget how to refresh my Nook. The user: CerebraNet said: Good for them. The user: CerebraNet said: FBI still has many criminals in the organisation. The user: CerebraNet said:  Lot of good college degree requirements does. The user: street said: People have broke into the FBI before, but not for a long time. The user: street said: Unless there was an inside job. ", "max_tokens": 350}','_max_body_size' => undef,'_uri' => bless( do{\(my $o = 'https://api.cohere.ai/v1/chat')}, 'URI::https' ),'_headers' => bless( {'x-client-name' => 'Franklin','user-agent' => 'libwww-perl/6.68','content-type' => 'application/json','authorization' => 'bearer jsIgap1Q************************2au0dV3Y','content-length' => 1715,'::std_case' => {'if-ssl-cert-subject' => 'If-SSL-Cert-Subject','x-client-name' => 'X-Client-Name'},'accept' => 'application/json'}, 'HTTP::Headers' ),'_uri_canonical' => $VAR1->{'_request'}{'_uri'},'_method' => 'POST'}, 'HTTP::Request' ),'_rc' => '200','_protocol' => 'HTTP/1.1','_content' => '{"response_id":"7b95c93e-f747-4681-a260-aff6ef227fde","text":"I can only speculate on why CerebraNet feels US schools do not help students decide between trade school and university. However, I can provide some possible reasons:\\n\\n1. Focus on Academic Excellence: Schools may prioritize academic excellence and college preparation curricula, which could inadvertently portray university as the preferred path. Teachers may feel pressure to prepare students for college entrance exams and applications, potentially neglecting the promotion of trade schools as a viable option.\\n\\n2. Societal Perception: There may be a general societal perception that university degrees are more prestigious or superior to skills learned in trade schools. This perception could influence how guidance counselors and teachers advise students, often pushing them towards the university route.\\n\\n3. Lack of Information: Schools might not have up-to-date or sufficient information about local trade school options, requirements, and career outcomes. This lack of knowledge could result in a bias towards university education, as counselors may feel more confident directing students down a path they know better.\\n\\n4. Funding and Resources: Trade schools and vocational programs often require specialized equipment and resources, which can be costly for educational institutions to provide. Schools may need to allocate funds to other essential operations, neglecting the development of robust trade programs.\\n\\n5. Career Counseling Resources: The availability of comprehensive career counseling services can vary greatly between schools. Some schools may lack the resources, time, or trained personnel to provide individualized guidance to help students make informed decisions about their post-secondary paths.\\n\\n\\nRemember, these are potential reasons and may not reflect the actual sentiments of CerebraNet or the reality of the educational system in the United States.","generation_id":"9605c2e8-16da-40ea-b29f-9af5b14f04fc","chat_history":[{"role":"USER","message":"Channel #2600: The user: street said: People have broke into the FBI before, but not for a long time. "},{"role":"CHATBOT","message":"I have no opinion on the matter, but it seems like CerebraNet supports the attempt."},{"role":"USER","message":"CerebraNet asked: Why do US schools not help students decide if trade school or university is better"},{"role":"CHATBOT","message":"I can only speculate on why CerebraNet feels US schools do not help students decide between trade school and university. However, I can provide some possible reasons:\\n\\n1. Focus on Academic Excellence: Schools may prioritize academic excellence and college preparation curricula, which could inadvertently portray university as the preferred path. Teachers may feel pressure to prepare students for college entrance exams and applications, potentially neglecting the promotion of trade schools as a viable option.\\n\\n2. Societal Perception: There may be a general societal perception that university degrees are more prestigious or superior to skills learned in trade schools. This perception could influence how guidance counselors and teachers advise students, often pushing them towards the university route.\\n\\n3. Lack of Information: Schools might not have up-to-date or sufficient information about local trade school options, requirements, and career outcomes. This lack of knowledge could result in a bias towards university education, as counselors may feel more confident directing students down a path they know better.\\n\\n4. Funding and Resources: Trade schools and vocational programs often require specialized equipment and resources, which can be costly for educational institutions to provide. Schools may need to allocate funds to other essential operations, neglecting the development of robust trade programs.\\n\\n5. Career Counseling Resources: The availability of comprehensive career counseling services can vary greatly between schools. Some schools may lack the resources, time, or trained personnel to provide individualized guidance to help students make informed decisions about their post-secondary paths.\\n\\n\\nRemember, these are potential reasons and may not reflect the actual sentiments of CerebraNet or the reality of the educational system in the United States."}],"finish_reason":"COMPLETE","token_count":{"prompt_tokens":426,"response_tokens":322,"total_tokens":748,"billed_tokens":732},"meta":{"api_version":{"version":"1"},"billed_units":{"input_tokens":410,"output_tokens":322}}}','_max_body_size' => undef,'_msg' => 'OK','_headers' => bless( {'expires' => 'Thu, 01 Jan 1970 00:00:00 UTC','client-ssl-cert-subject' => '/CN=api.cohere.com','x-debug-trace-id' => '6b5cd0fe4503e018a29269f32c07d1a8','x-envoy-upstream-service-time' => '3186','client-ssl-cert-issuer' => '/C=US/O=Let\'s Encrypt/CN=R3','client-ssl-cipher' => 'TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384','vary' => 'Origin','x-accel-expires' => '0','client-response-num' => 1,'date' => 'Tue, 02 Apr 2024 04:26:16 GMT','num_chars' => '1865','connection' => 'close','via' => '1.1 google','cache-control' => 'no-cache, no-store, no-transform, must-revalidate, private, max-age=0','::std_case' => {'num_chars' => 'Num_chars','client-response-num' => 'Client-Response-Num','access-control-expose-headers' => 'Access-Control-Expose-Headers','client-ssl-version' => 'Client-SSL-Version','client-date' => 'Client-Date','alt-svc' => 'Alt-Svc','num_tokens' => 'Num_tokens','client-ssl-cert-subject' => 'Client-SSL-Cert-Subject','client-transfer-encoding