rhaps for the hassle they gave me lifetime Emerald or something. . The user: Zed said: just use google photos. The user: Zed said: imgur is great tho. The user: CerebraNet said: I notice some people in #2600 use Imgur. The user: Zed said: if you dont want google snooping your shit. The user: Zed said: cuz they will. ", "max_tokens": 350}','_uri_canonical' => $VAR1->{'_request'}{'_uri'},'_max_body_size' => undef,'_headers' => bless( {'user-agent' => 'libwww-perl/6.68','::std_case' => {'x-client-name' => 'X-Client-Name','if-ssl-cert-subject' => 'If-SSL-Cert-Subject'},'content-type' => 'application/json','content-length' => 2177,'x-client-name' => 'Franklin','authorization' => 'bearer jsIgap1Q************************2au0dV3Y','accept' => 'application/json'}, 'HTTP::Headers' ),'_method' => 'POST'}, 'HTTP::Request' ),'_rc' => '200','_content' => '{"response_id":"68e12c89-6065-4c7b-8453-a86dc7b87929","text":"Beep... Yes, it is possible for companies like Google to access and analyze the photos you share online, especially if you are using their platforms and services. They may employ various techniques, including image recognition and data mining, to extract information from your photos for various purposes, such as advertising, user profiling, or even improving their algorithms. This practice is often done without your explicit consent, and it raises concerns about privacy and data ownership. To protect your privacy, consider using alternative services that prioritize user privacy and encryption or look into methods to obscure or anonymize your photos before sharing them online.","generation_id":"b118a361-4c81-43ad-9f71-50de5da46f14","chat_history":[{"role":"USER","message":"Channel #2600: The user: Zed said: if you dont want google snooping your shit. "},{"role":"CHATBOT","message":"Beep... Affirmative, master oxagast. I am an IRC bot designed to respond to your queries and provide assistance. My current uptime is continuous, and I am always active in this channel unles