eeding only reinforces dominant genetic trates, genetic deceases only occur when both partners have the same one, which is unlikely to occur with a small group. It also stunts evolution though, but think of dog breeding, sure you have some 50/50s of well known breeds but compair every pure-bred to the muts and the amount of genetic diversity there.... The user: zyme said: On the subject of Greek mythology, Zeus would change his appearance often when he had affairs with mortals. The user: zyme said: Franklin: Isnt that right about zeus?. The user: zyme said: Franklin: What other greek gods could do that, do we know?. ", "max_tokens": 350}','_method' => 'POST'}, 'HTTP::Request' ),'_content' => '{"response_id":"8e1a4669-d948-4191-9464-78ab715b1f07","text":"Apollo is the son of Zeus and Leto, and the twin brother of Artemis. He is known as the god of music, poetry, archery, plague, healing, light, prophecy, and knowledge. While Apollo is not known for changing his appearance frequently like Zeus, there are instances in Greek mythology where he does take on different forms. One example is when Apollo pursued the nymph Daphne, who did not return his affections. To escape Apollo\'s advances, Daphne transformed into a laurel tree. In his grief, Apollo then transformed himself into a laurel tree as well, so that he could forever be with Daphne. So while Apollo may not have been a shape-shifter on the same scale as Zeus, he did have the ability to change his form when the situation called for it.","generation_id":"eb327b7a-6773-4aea-8925-209c6e7a0ea2","chat_history":[{"role":"USER","message":"Channel #2600: The user: zyme said: Franklin: Isnt that right about zeus?. "},{"role":"CHATBOT","message":"Many of the Greek gods had the ability to change their appearance. Some examples include:  - Aphrodite, the goddess of love and beauty, who could change her appearance to seduce mortals. - Hermes, the messenger god, who could take on different forms to deliver messages discreetly. - Poseidon, the god of the sea, who could change his appearance to interact with mortals at sea. - Artemis, "},{"role":"USER","message":"zyme asked: What about apollo?"},{"role":"CHATBOT","message":"Apollo is the son of Zeus and Leto, and the twin brother of Artemis. He is known as the god of music, poetry, archery, plague, healing, light, prophecy, and knowledge. While Apollo is not known for changing his appearance frequently like Zeus, there are instances in Greek mythology where he does take on different forms. One example is when Apollo pursued the nymph Daphne, who did not return his affections. To escape Apollo\'s advances, Daphne transformed into a laurel tree. In his grief, Apollo then transformed himself into a laurel tree as well, so that he could forever be with Daphne. So while Apollo may not have been a shape-shifter on the same scale as Zeus, he did have the ability to change his form when the situation called for it."}],"finish_reason":"COMPLETE","meta":{"api_version":{"version":"1"},"billed_units":{"input_tokens":469,"output_tokens":156},"tokens":{"input_tokens":483,"output_tokens":156}}}','_max_body_size' => undef,'_headers' => bless( {'client-date' => 'Fri, 12 Apr 2024 10:48:22 GMT','num_chars' => '2124','::std_case' => {'client-date' => 'Client-Date','client-ssl-cert-issuer' => 'Client-SSL-Cert-Issuer','num_tokens' => 'Num_tokens','num_chars' => 'Num_chars','client-response-num' => 'Client-Response-Num','x-debug-trace-id' => 'X-Debug-Trace-Id','client-transfer-encoding' => 'Client-Transfer-Encoding','x-envoy-upstream-service-time' => 'X-Envoy-Upstream-Service-Time','access-control-expose-headers' => 'Access-Control-Expose-Headers','client-peer' => 'Client-Peer','client-ssl-cipher' => 'Client-SSL-Cipher','client-ssl-version' => 'Client-SSL-Version','client-ssl-cert-subject' => 'Client-SSL-Cert-Subject','x-accel-expires' => 'X-Accel-Expires','alt-svc' => 'Alt-Svc','client-ssl-socket-class' => 'Client-SSL-Socket-Class'},'x-debug-trace-id' => 'c21ea98